24,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F92f7c826-0b02-4891-9750-5d347a3f85ed_1000x562.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!nXao!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F92f7c826-0b02-4891-9750-5d347a3f85ed_1000x562.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!nXao!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F92f7c826-0b02-4891-9750-5d347a3f85ed_1000x562.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!nXao!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F92f7c826-0b02-4891-9750-5d347a3f85ed_1000x562.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!nXao!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F92f7c826-0b02-4891-9750-5d347a3f85ed_1000x562.png\" width=\"1000\" height=\"562\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/92f7c826-0b02-4891-9750-5d347a3f85ed_1000x562.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:false,&quot;imageSize&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;height&quot;:562,&quot;width&quot;:1000,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:1000,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!nXao!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F92f7c826-0b02-4891-9750-5d347a3f85ed_1000x562.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!nXao!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F92f7c826-0b02-4891-9750-5d347a3f85ed_1000x562.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!nXao!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F92f7c826-0b02-4891-9750-5d347a3f85ed_1000x562.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!nXao!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F92f7c826-0b02-4891-9750-5d347a3f85ed_1000x562.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>If you want to see where this leads on the language side, Babylon and HAT, which <strong>Juan Fumero</strong> presented at JavaOne 2026 (<a href=\"https://inside.java/2026/07/30/under-the-hat-empowering-gpu-acceleration-for-java/\">Under the HAT</a>), use code-reflection APIs to translate sections of Java programs into CUDA and OpenCL. Java as a description something gets generated from, again. But that is a topic for its own edition.</p><p>Some context to close: the company behind Gradle renamed itself in June from Gradle Technologies to <a href=\"https://blog.gradle.org/the-company-formerly-known-as-gradle\">Develocity</a>, after its commercial product. The build tool does not change its name, its owner or its licence, and \"Gradle by Develocity\" in search results is, in their own words, a fixed naming bug. There was no acquisition.</p><div><hr></div><p><strong>PS:</strong> If the first section left you wanting more Ślusarski, his older piece on <a href=\"https://krzysztofslusarski.github.io/2020/11/10/humongous.html\">humongous objects</a> is the natural prequel. His own note on the site's front page fits this edition's theme too: he writes that since 2026 he uses models as a tool in most of his investigations, and points specifically at the table translating assembly into pseudocode in this article as AI-generated.</p><p><strong>PS2:</strong> JDK 27 next week, I promise, and this time with a date on the calendar: GA falls on September 15. And if anyone fancies talking about write barriers in person, Confitura is on September 25 and 26 at the ADN Conference Center on Grzybowska 56 in Warsaw.</p><div class=\"subscription-widget-wrap-editor\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://www.jvm-weekly.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe&quot;,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"SubscribeWidgetToDOM\"><div class=\"subscription-widget show-subscribe\"><div class=\"preamble\"><p class=\"cta-caption\">Thanks for reading JVM Weekly! Subscribe for free to receive new posts and support my work.</p></div><form class=\"subscription-widget-subscribe\"><input type=\"email\" class=\"email-input\" name=\"email\" placeholder=\"Type your email…\" tabindex=\"-1\"><input type=\"submit\" class=\"button primary\" value=\"Subscribe\"><div class=\"fake-input-wrapper\"><div class=\"fake-input\"></div><div class=\"fake-button\"></div></div></form></div></div>","has_dynamic_content":false,"truncated_body_text":"A week without the JDK in the lead role (JDK 27 ships on September 15 and gets its own edition, relax). Instead, three pieces from the last few weeks that share one question: how much of what runs on your JVM did you actually write. The answer, as usual, is \"less than you think\", but this time I have three very concrete examples, one from each layer.","wordcount":2783,"post_preview_limit":null,"language":"en","postTags":[],"postCountryBlocks":[],"headlineTest":null,"coverImagePalette":{"Vibrant":{"rgb":[246,127,68],"population":398},"DarkVibrant":{"rgb":[4,124,60],"population":1201},"LightVibrant":{"rgb":[98,227,132],"population":33},"Muted":{"rgb":[86,165,125],"population":74},"DarkMuted":{"rgb":[97,78,62],"population":249},"LightMuted":{"rgb":[179,208,191],"population":39}},"publishedBylines":[{"id":73551664,"name":"Artur Skowronski","handle":"arturskowronski","photo_url":"https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/02ec8807-299f-42d2-bcde-168795228629_2362x2362.png","bio":"Head of Java / Kotlin Engineering at VirtusLab","profile_set_up_at":"2022-04-25T10:31:27.502Z","reader_installed_at":"2022-05-12T11:28:55.290Z","publicationUsers":[{"id":802994,"user_id":73551664,"publication_id":862586,"role":"admin","